    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1070">

                <pb facs="1244" n="1048" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1048"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/7–3145: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1070<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-31T20:00:00+02:00">July 31, 1945—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4640. Re this Embassy’s memo July 21<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1070-f1"/> pertaining
                    to control by Allies to be exercised in Greece during forthcoming elections,
                    memo has been received from Foreign Office dated July 20 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">30</hi>].<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1070-f2"/></p>
                <p>Confirming my 4395 July 21<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1070-f3"/> this memo informs
                    Embassy that French Government accepts readily to participate in Four Power
                    control of these elections.</p>
                <p>French Foreign Office furthermore shares views of American Government re
                    necessity of keeping these consultations secret until answers of four interested
                    Governments are received and Greek Government informed officially.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
